<h2>Questions from Indianapolis property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does living in a historic district change my claim?</summary><div class="a"><p>It can. Locally designated districts may require approved materials or methods for exterior repairs. Where those requirements raise the cost, ordinance or law coverage and the amount of loss can both be affected.</p></div></details><details><summary>My Indianapolis home has had two hail claims in five years. Will that hurt?</summary><div class="a"><p>Prior claims often lead carriers to argue that damage is old. Dated photos, repair invoices from the earlier claim and storm-specific evidence help show what is new.</p></div></details></div>
